+\paragraph{catalog\_v4 against the pp-trained arm on pp events (2026-10-29).}\label{par:v4_vs_pp} The question the
+pp study was opened for (the user, 2026-10-26: what mattered most was how training on catalog\_v4 compares to training
+on pp collisions, on data generated like pp collisions): does catalog\_v4 serve pp events as well as training on them?
+No new run: the two catalog\_v4 Muon runs of par.~\ref{par:v4_vs_v3} against the pp-trained arm of par.\ The
+pp-trained arm (\code{FA-ccin2p3-e786bd74}, its read completed by \code{FA-ccin2p3-982b5a14}), on the same $13$\,TeV pp
+pools of the $1396$ hadronic tree classes, the same $2000$ validation events per class, all at $4264$ steps and their
+best checkpoint (\code{analysis/catalog\_v4/pp\_trained\_compare.py}, Fig.~\ref{fig:v4_vs_pp}). Two checks pass on
+every class: the reads score the same events (the variance of each catalog\_v4 and catalog\_v3 Muon read's target
+equals the pp-trained arm's within $10^{-3}$ relative, the sorted events match the pool's, and no pp pool was rebuilt
+in between), and the split into the events inside and outside catalog\_v3's window coverage is one definition (both
+come from the same mask; the share inside agrees exactly). Groups as in par.~\ref{par:v4_vs_v3}: the $578$ classes
+trained in both catalogs and the $180$ held out in both, no $b$ (the pp pools have catalog\_v3's $4.7$\,GeV $b$, on
+which the pp-trained arm trained and catalog\_v4 never did). Every number is the median over classes of a per-class MSE
+ratio of $\log|\mathcal M|^2$, catalog\_v4 as the geometric mean of its two seeds. The two sides do not share an
+optimizer: the pp-trained arm and its window-trained control are AdamW, one seed each; catalog\_v4's runs are Muon,
+which on these pp pools reads catalog\_v3's windows at $0.26$ (trained classes) and $0.28$ (held out) of AdamW's error
+(par.~\ref{par:v3_muon}). Two readings follow.
+\begin{itemize}
+  \item \emph{Directly, catalog\_v4 with Muon against the pp-trained arm with AdamW.} On the classes trained in both,
